  "filled_passage": "My uncle wanted to take some young plants to (1) his old friend in another town. He had (2) lost the address and thought he would have to cancel the visit. Then he remembered that it might be written on a card in his desk.\n\nThe town was much (3) farther away than I expected. We put the plants in a box and covered them with paper. Uncle held the smallest one (4) gently while I placed a rolled towel around its pot. We did not close the top of the box (5) because the leaves were taller than the sides.\n\nUncle's friend was a very (6) friendly person. He met us at the bus station and carried the box to his house. As soon as we arrived, Uncle (7) found the card in his coat pocket. He had put it there when he went to look for the desk key, then forgotten about it.\n\nI knew that it was the (8) third house on the street because the first two had blue doors. We went in (9) without knocking because Uncle's friend was right beside us. His garden was much larger than ours, with a covered area for young plants. I was (10) surprised to see how many different shapes of leaf there were. We left our box beside the path and spent the afternoon looking around.",
